07/14/26|07/14/26||CDT|0|F|Y|Chicago|IL|41.8410|-87.6745|OZONE||Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups|Yes|(Discussion Issued 7/14/26 11:30am) Currently USG Ozone forecasts are in place for Chicago Area AQI forecast sectors for today July 14th and for Wednesday July 15th. Additionally, model guidance is indicating the potential for wildfire smoke reaching parts of northern Illinois by Thursday, July 16th.  Surface smoke may reach northeastern Illinois by early Thursday and gradually expand from the Chicago region towards Rockford and surrounding area throughout the day.  Daily PM2.5 forecasts for these areas are set at Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups (USG) for Thursday but may need adjusted depending on model updates and on what levels of smoke verify Wednesday north of Illinois.  There is also potential for smoke that negatively impacts AQI to linger in parts of Illinois Friday and into the weekend.  Areas impacted will routinely be assessed and AQI forecasts revised as needed over the next several days. Note, NowCast AQI readings may show categories higher than the daily forecast to help identify periods of higher 1-hour PM2.5/smoke.  For a description of the differences between daily AQI forecasts and NowCast AQI, visit https://www.airnow.gov/aqi/aqi-basics/using-air-quality-index/ .  Those with air quality concerns or outdoor plans can periodically check current NowCast readings or sign up for EnviroFlash alerts on AirNow.gov|Illinois EPA
