07/14/26|07/14/26||EDT|0|F|Y|Philadelphia|PA|39.9500|-75.1510|OZONE|80|Moderate|No|***AN EXTREME HEAT WARNING IS IN EFFECT FROM 10 AM EDT WEDNESDAY THROUGH 8 PM EDT  WEDNESDAY*** Current Conditions at 2 p.m. EDT this Tuesday afternoon: Fine particle (PM2.5) and ozone remain in the moderate range. A smoke event is on the way beginning Wednesday night and continuing into Thursday with a dense plume expected to affect our area. In addition to the expected poor air quality, the heat will continue for a couple more days. Here are the forecast details:  ***  Wednesday’s forecast: High heat and degrading air quality is expected Wednesday with high temperatures close to 100 degrees with heat indices of 105. Ozone will climb into the high moderate range, with a couple of hours of code ORANGE concentrations. PM2.5 will remain moderate through the day, but then increase to unhealthy levels overnight.  ***  Extended forecast: Poor air quality is possible Thursday and Friday, and air quality alerts may be needed during this period as the flow turns into the northwest and allows wildfire smoke in southern Canada and the north-central U.S. to move into the state. In addition, ozone levels will also be affected by the low level smoke. The next chance for thunderstorms or showers will not occur until Saturday, with the air quality improving some with the precipitation.---McAuliffe|Pennsylvania Dept. of Environmental Protection
